  "findings": [
    "Category packages embedded JSZip, fflate, fast-xml-parser, docx-preview and Three.js, leading to duplicate implementations when combined. Declared npm dependencies and their subpaths are now left for the application bundler to share.",
    "PDF library worker URL was Base64-encoded. Its existing worker is now emitted as its original MJS file.",
    "iWork used full protobufjs despite JSON schemas. It now uses the light runtime and initializes the schema on demand, allowing consumers using only worker viewers to eliminate the main-thread parser.",
    "Three.js vendors the same fflate 0.8.2 implementation. Source demo/standalone builds now resolve that code to the shared fflate dependency.",
    "RAW image duplicate syn versions are build-time procedural macros, not runtime WASM duplication. STEP has mixed runtime itertools versions and build-time derive/syn versions; no changes were made to these or HEIF in this audit."
  ],
  "artifacts": "Intermediate builds are under ignored tmp/format-size-audit; production library and standalone builds are regenerated separately.",
